# Summary
The commit introduces a reachable cleanup gap for streaming UploadPart reuploads: old chunk manifests are deleted before shard cleanup and the cleanup lookup uses old generation version_id instead of the new staging sentinel, so stale shards are never removed.
With streaming UploadPart enabled, chunk manifests are committed with a u64::MAX staging version_id and commit_stream_part deletes prior chunk rows by upload_id before the coordinator attempts cleanup. The cleanup logic then queries get_multipart_part_chunks using the old generation version_id, which no longer matches the sentinel and no longer exists in metadata because the rows were already deleted. As a result, re-uploading the same part leaves the previous chunk shards on disk. An authenticated client can repeatedly reupload a single part to accumulate orphaned shard data and exhaust storage, bypassing the expected per-part/object size limits.

# Reviewer note
This report is old in terminology, but the bug shape still appears to be
present in the current tree.

Terminology changes since the original report:
- `chunk` manifests are now `segment` manifests
- `multipart_part_chunks` is now `multipart_part_segments`
- `get_multipart_part_chunks` is now `get_multipart_part_segments`
- the affected coordinator path is now `finalize_stream_part` in
  `crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs`

Current-tree mapping of the same issue:
- `finalize_stream_part` still commits new streamed-part segments first and
  only then attempts best-effort cleanup of the prior streamed-part shards
  ([crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs#L10161)).
- `commit_stream_part` still deletes prior `multipart_part_segments` rows for
  the upload+part before inserting the new rows
  ([crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs#L6366)).
- The subsequent cleanup lookup still fetches by the old generation's
  `version_id`, via `get_multipart_part_segments`, which filters strictly on
  `version_id`
  ([crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs#L10193),
  [crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs](/home/justin/src/github.com/justincormack/argmin/crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs#L6534)).

So the report should be read as referring to streamed-part segment manifests in
the current implementation rather than the older chunk-based names.

# Resolution
Fixed in commit `a939d4c` (`Fix streamed upload part shard cleanup`).

The shipped fix updates the storage contract so `commit_stream_part` returns the
prior `multipart_part_segments` rows it displaced inside the same transaction,
before deleting those metadata rows. The coordinator's `finalize_stream_part`
path now uses that returned segment set for best-effort shard cleanup after the
commit instead of trying to rediscover the old rows with a post-commit
`get_multipart_part_segments(... old version_id ...)` lookup that could never
succeed after the delete.

Regression coverage added with the fix:
- storage-level coverage now asserts reuploads return the displaced streamed-part
  segment manifests
- coordinator-level coverage now verifies that reuploading a streamed part
  deletes the prior segment shard files from disk

